{"title":"2000 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 12 Problems\">2000 AMC 12 #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">2000 AMC 10 #11</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Meta-solving)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Meta-solving)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_by_RMM_Club\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video by RMM Club</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two different prime numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen. When their sum is subtracted from their product, which of the following numbers could be obtained?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77fafaa9b651ef1885cda88e2ef19aefaadbd326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 21 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 60 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 119 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 180 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 231$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Meta-solving.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Meta-solving)\">Solution 1 (Meta-solving)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Meta-solving)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Both prime numbers are odd, so their product is odd and their sum is even.  Therefore, the obtained number is odd, and (B) and (D) are incorrect. \n</p><p>The largest two prime numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the obtained number must be less than the product of the two primes.  So any number obtained is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/02853993e4296782cf97b17d908606db9116ac66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\cdot 17 = 221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />, so (E) is too large and therefore incorrect.\n</p><p>If the prime numbers chosen are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, then the required difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25fc6db973bcc5fb56b938d6f12ae5c24c911103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a - 1)(b - 1) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"20\" /> so the minimum value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce1d954c30c34db8baf82b1535c8370070d5380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 6 - 1 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> so (A) is incorrect.\n</p><p>This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9b1e6b827b373d1ef5d99e865cb1a3f23165de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 119}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />, which is correct as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c011a8a5f50430e3eded736f9253e5d0ae620899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot 13 - (11+13) = 119$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the two primes.  \n</p><p>Then the obtained number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebb5a4ad851a85ecdb4e6bd08107404e8747d69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq-(p+q)=pq-p-q=pq-p-q+1-1=(p-1)(q-1)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"532\" height=\"20\" /> by Simon's favorite factoring trick. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0100a4dffd902b9459e7a3b2c024bf41f73893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)(q-1)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> must be odd, so (A), (B), and (D) are incorrect.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4feca6ed02dae19ad7181846b090f18f2100408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)(q-1)-1 = 231$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1050bba72cb5fb21d4dfc96658e74bea43a4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)(q-1) = 232 = 2^3 \\cdot 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"234\" height=\"21\" />.  So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55af207869f43d97328748a5cb85274095a6a935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, and thus either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which is too large.  So (E) is incorrect.\n</p><p>This leaves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9b1e6b827b373d1ef5d99e865cb1a3f23165de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 119}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />, which is obtained if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d581cb3653184f302b2d5c147b8709695dec285f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p, q) = (11, 13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~JerryZYang, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p3bwMuK1RUM?si=fxoNgkv-Ue31mqCk&amp;t=53\">https://youtu.be/p3bwMuK1RUM?si=fxoNgkv-Ue31mqCk&amp;t=53</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_by_RMM_Club\">Video by RMM Club</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video by RMM Club\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ddE5GO1RNLw&amp;t=1s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ddE5GO1RNLw&amp;t=1s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xmiLZVy0JVM?si=DJitB2xBZOuyMkWu\">https://youtu.be/xmiLZVy0JVM?si=DJitB2xBZOuyMkWu</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 10\">2000 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\